# ============================================================================
# PROXMOX STORAGE POOL PREREQUISITES (CRITICAL)
# ============================================================================
#
# BEFORE running terraform apply, verify these storage pools exist in Proxmox:
#
# REQUIRED Storage Pool:
# - ssd: 500GB+ minimum (LVM-thin or SSD-based filesystem)
#   IMPORTANT: Must be LVM-thin, SSD, or ZFS. NOT a directory-based "local" pool.
#   Used by: ALL containers (BASTION01-02, DNS01-02, PROXY01-02, AUTHENTIK01-02, DOCKER01-02, PLEX01)
#
# ERROR Prevention:
# If you see: "storage 'local' does not support container directories"
#   → You need to create an SSD pool that is LVM-thin or SSD-based
#   → Directory-based storage pools CANNOT be used for containers
#
# To verify available storage pools:
# 1. Proxmox Web UI: Datacenter > Storage (check Status tab)
# 2. Via SSH to Proxmox node: pvesh get /storage
#
# To create the 'ssd' storage pool:
# - See terraform/README_STORAGE_POOLS.md for detailed instructions
# - Common pool types: LVM-thin (recommended), ZFS, or SSD filesystem mount
#
# If your storage pool has a different name (not 'ssd'):
# - Edit each module's variables.tf file
# - Update the storage_pool default value
# - Example: terraform/bastion01/variables.tf
#   storage_pool = "nvme"  (or your pool name)

# ============================================================================
# VM ID ALLOCATION SCHEMA (MUST BE UNIQUE)
# ============================================================================
#
# PhoenixStack uses these fixed VM IDs. If you need different IDs:
# 1. Edit each module's variables.tf file
# 2. Change the container_vmid default value
# 3. Ensure NO duplicate VM IDs
# 4. Run terraform plan to verify no conflicts
#
# Current allocation:
# 101: BASTION01 (Management & GitHub runner)
# 102: BASTION02 (Secondary bastion & GitHub runner)
# 103: DNS01 (DNS/PiHole server)
# 104: DNS02 (DNS/PiHole server secondary)
# 105: PROXY01 (Reverse proxy/Traefik)
# 106: [AVAILABLE]
# 107: AUTHENTIK01 (Identity provider)
# 108: AUTHENTIK02 (Identity provider secondary)
# 109: DOCKER01 (Container host)
# 110: DOCKER02 (Container host secondary)
# 111: PLEX01 (Media server)
# 112: SQL01 (PostgreSQL primary) - PLANNED
# 113: SQL02 (PostgreSQL standby) - PLANNED
#
# Reserved for future services:
# 114+: Additional services

# ============================================================================
# DEPLOYMENT VERIFICATION
# ============================================================================
#
# After terraform apply succeeds:
# 1. Check Proxmox Web UI - all 10 containers should be running
# 2. Verify IPs: ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 root@10.101.0.20 (BASTION01)
# 3. Verify all containers: for ip in 10.101.0.{20,21,22,23,25,30,201,202}; do ping -c 1 $ip; done
#
# If containers fail to start:
# - Check Proxmox > Node > LXC > Container > Status tab
# - Common issues:
#   * Storage pool doesn't exist (update variables.tf for that module)
#   * VM ID conflict (check for duplicate IDs across modules)
#   * Insufficient disk space (expand storage pool or reduce container sizes)
